{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/287549-plating-armor-with-iron-ways-to-do-it-without-iron-losing-its-properties","id":287549,"title":"Plating Armor with Iron - Ways to do it without iron losing its properties?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-20T06:47:42-07:00","id":287549,"title":"Plating Armor with Iron - Ways to do it without iron losing its properties?","content":"Basically, my assumption is that iron as second most stable element in universe (actually nickel-62 is more stable than iron, but it's also rare. Within my assumption it's even more effective than iron, but any artifact made for it will be rare enough to make it not as widespread as iron ones) thus it's an anathema to fluid reality that True Fae embody, and it also affects Spirits and Mages (the latter not in the sense of iron harming them, but certain artifacts made from cold iron could give enhanced resistance against Arcana effects).<br /> <br /> Hunter Conspiracy I craft makes use of Iron plated armors and suits, those enviromentally sealed being able to remarkably stave off effects of Hedge on mortals (before you ask how they get there, they maintain positive relationship with freeholds, especially Summer Court as they share similar militant attitude towards the threat of Gentry). Protective Iron artifacts like that could be part of Endowments.<br /> <br /> The question is, what could be a method of covering such suits/armors with Iron plating without it losing its anti-magic properties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:31:59-07:00","id":287827,"title":"","content":"Well, important question:<br /> <br /> Is the scientific explanation of why iron is so important metaphysically true in your take on this, or just the explanation this Conspiracy uses since they don't actually understand the Fae completely? Are we throwing out the CtL books explanations about why iron is important (which also serves as the basis for why iron has to be treated in a specific way)? What does any of this have to do with spirits and mages (many of whom have affinities that have no assumptions about not working on iron effectively as written and don't give any shits about its atomic structure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:57:07-07:00","id":287835,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the scientific explanation of why iron is so important metaphysically true in your take on this, or just the explanation this Conspiracy uses since they don't actually understand the Fae completely? Are we throwing out the CtL books explanations about why iron is important (which also serves as the basis for why iron has to be treated in a specific way)? What does any of this have to do with spirits and mages (many of whom have affinities that have no assumptions about not working on iron effectively as written and don't give any shits about its atomic structure). </div> </div> </div>1) On meta level it is, but the Conspiracy generally buys into occult explanations and is not aware of why exactly Iron works on Fae, just it works and gets things done, some have their own interpretations, some share views of those Changelings they are familiar with. While they started melding technology into their worldview, they are Conspiracy going back to medieval ages and steeped into folklore on Fae.<br /> <br /> 2) It's my twist on &quot;The Foe of All Unreason&quot;. As iron is one of more static existences at its core it came to conceptually embody mundanity not only because it's inherently stable element but because it's also common enough (throwing away nickel-62 from this equation, not common enough to embody the concept).<br /> <br /> 3) Here are rules I got inspired by:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Cold iron has the same effect on any sort of magical defenses that it does on fae magic. Vampiric Disciplines, werewolf Gifts, the Arcana of mages and the alchemical Transmutations of Prometheans are powerless to resist the sundering power of cold iron (NOTE: Here is where I started thinking if cold iron shaped into likeness of an armor can have defensive properties)<br /> \u2022 Most supernaturals, just as changelings, do not take aggravated damage from hand-forged iron. However,beings of a \u201cpure\u201d magical nature akin to theGentry (such as spirits, ghosts, Abyssal entities and qashmallim) may suffer aggravated damage from handforged iron.<br /> \u2022 Hand-forged iron that is improved or forged in any way with magic (such as Contracts of Artifice or the Smith\u2019s kith blessing) becomes immediately and permanently treated as cold iron. Cold iron improved or forged with magic loses all its beneficial effects against the supernatural.<br /> <br /> I went with &quot;technobabble&quot; because ultimately I'm expanding my personal canon into interstellar tier, so a little nod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, important question: </div> </div> </div>Oh, and thanks for asking, I always appreciate &quot;nitpicking&quot; like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T14:53:56-07:00","id":287989,"title":"","content":"If you're going with &quot;The Foe of All Unreason&quot; option, then the standard issues with handling iron all still apply. In some senses it is actually easier to do things like iron armor if you can work iron appropriately, because you could do something like scale, lamellar, or plated mail style (where you just need to be able to reliably produce relatively small and simple shapes). Then you can lace them over the environmental suit and use that to replace the padding layers used in traditional armors. This is going to be much easier to do and avoid depowering the iron compared to trying to make full plate armor with it. Though obviously this armor would provide less actual protection from damage than full plate.<br /> <br /> Though I would be extremely hesitant to apply &quot;The Foe of All Unreason&quot; in anything but a pure Changeling game (though Changeling + Hunter I can see). Forcing the other supernaturals to follow this is kind of taking a massive dump on their metaphysics. &quot;It's so not special it degrades magic&quot; really doesn't make any sense in the other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T10:09:51-07:00","id":288659,"title":"","content":"You want a Hedge Encounter Suit?<br /> <br /> Sew hematite fragments into the fabric of a hazmat suit. Draw apotropaics all over the thing, and fill the air filter with symbolically pure herbs and flowers. Finally, learn as many prayers and warding rhymes as you can, in case any of them <i>work.</i><br /> If you can get your hands on telluric or meteoric iron, work it flat with a hammer, and then attach it to your suit by nail and glue. Make sure it's not too heavy, because you need to be able to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T11:39:01-07:00","id":288712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I would be extremely hesitant TO APPLY &quot;The Foe of All Unreason&quot; in anything but a pure Changeling game (though Changeling + Hunter I can see). Forcing the other supernaturals to follow this is kind of taking a massive dump on their metaphysics. &quot;It's so not special it degrades magic&quot; really doesn't make any sense in the other game lines. </div> </div> </div>The conspiracy is primarily for Changeling/Hunter games, so don't worry. Probably I can come up with alternatives in case of integrating them with wider stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:20:39-07:00","id":288754,"title":"","content":"How thick do you want the iron?<br /> <br /> Theoretically, you could mould the iron into any shape you want with a strong enough magnetic field; I'm thinking 2.5 cm thick sheets (flattens through magnetism).<br /> <br /> Because then you just need some method of cutting it, and then you can apply it to a mold.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the mold would look a bit like a dress mold, with a powerful electromagnet at the core. As it powers up, the iron would deform to the right shape. You just need to stop it periodically to adjust the layering of the iron, use a hammer for the final shaping, and then bolt it together.<br /> <br /> You need about 1.9 m<sup>2</sup> of this plating to cover an average adult male; that comes out to about 37.5 kg (a bit under 87 lbs) spread over your body. Once you've learned to move in it, you shouldn't have much of a problem. Now, the question is whether you want to layer the rest of your armor <i>on top</i> of that, or <i>under</i> it. Because if the latter, it'll get a few kilos heavier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:24:50-07:00","id":288762,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if moulding it through electromagnetic things would let it retain mystical properties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:39:15-07:00","id":288779,"title":"","content":"It totally would; you are neither heating it (well, no more than you would be if you were hitting it <i>really hard</i> with a hammer) nor applying magic to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:57:02-07:00","id":288810,"title":"","content":"My biggest caveat would be, for me, I would not want the armor to make the PCs feel safe, or their players feel safe, in the Hedge or dealing with the Gentry. It can mitigate it somewhat, but trying to set something up to make dealing with either safe to me runs against the feel of the game, for whatever that is worth to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:02:14-07:00","id":288814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My biggest caveat would be, for me, I would not want the armor to make the PCs feel safe, or their players feel safe, in the Hedge or dealing with the Gentry. It can mitigate it somewhat, but trying to set something up to make dealing with either safe to me runs against the feel of the game, for whatever that is worth to you. </div> </div> </div>1) Requires 5 Status<br /> 2) Not completely fool proof and things can happen. Some of Hunters may be... eccentric. On even suffer from minor changes to their bodies.<br /> <br /> If Hunter might go &quot;natural&quot; Changeling thanks to overexposure due to failure of protection and being stranded, and is rescued back from Hedge (not Arcadia), I think the group will simply tell now mechanically not a mortal to just apply to sympathetic/allied freehold, no hard feelings. Status converted into Goodwill equivalent with the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-21-2014, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:16:11-07:00","id":288821,"title":"","content":"The requires 5 status is not really relevant to my point.<br /> <br /> My point is, are you adding something to make them safe, or feel safe, in the Hedge or safe from the Gentry, ie can they travel the Hedge safely or approach the Gentry without fear?<br /> <br /> If the answer is &quot;No, they are safe-er, in the sense a Fireman's gear makes him safer in a burning house and he is a fool to go without it&quot; then I have no issue at all. If they can mostly travel the hedge and deal with the Gentry without fear from behind this Aegis, it is problematic thematically.<br /> <br /> And if you don't care about themes or such, the above does not matter.<br /> <br /> None of this is snark or saying anything sucks, just my view of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:25:00-07:00","id":288825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of this is snark or saying anything sucks, just my view of it. </div> </div> </div>No, I actually appreciate that. The idea is still in early stage, so basically every opinion is welcomed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the answer is &quot;No, they are safe-er, in the sense a Fireman's gear makes him safer in a burning house and he is a fool to go without it&quot; then I have no issue at all. If they can mostly travel the hedge and deal with the Gentry without fear from behind this Aegis, it is problematic thematically. </div> </div> </div>More in this sense, because I hold that Gentry are one of scariest antagonists in NWoD, and the group is basically motivated with fear of Gentry having their own way in mortal world. Add paranoia mutually shared with their Changeling allies that Loyalists and/or people manipulated by them may hide within their ranks, and there is recipe for mental deterioration (Avenger Slasher murdering people whom he suspects of being fetches? Possible).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:31:49-07:00","id":288926,"title":"","content":"Any counter-reasoning to my last post?<br /> <br /> I only ask because iron armor shaped by magnetism just <i>sounds</i> cool to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:50:29-07:00","id":289029,"title":"","content":"Fae and iron is a result of some Contract according to the line's lore. Cold iron isn't necessarily all that pure. It does have a very low carbon content. It can be welded to softer steel, beaten into sheets or drawn into wire (if it is very pure iron). The welding would mess with the mojo at the joints, but you might be able to creatively weld it chemically or magically so the joint is on the inside so it wouldn't matter.<br /> <br /> The iron can be crafted into common types of archaic armor like plate, chain or scale. The biggest problem is it isn't as strong as steel and Gentry can use steel weapons. Iron on the outside would be effective against magic, but not as much against mundane weapon attacks. It might help with Gentry magic but be vulnerable to Goblin attacks. Just a point to consider.<br /> <br /> I think magnetism would be fine as long as the force was not stronger than the hammer. Cold iron typically has impurities in the form of strings within the piece of metal so too much force would crack and break the piece of iron. I don't see any advantage to magnetism, but if you just want to use it as a replacement for cold working (similar craft time) then it sounds fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:50:25-07:00","id":289824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fae and iron is a result of some Contract according to the line's lore. </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily as Foe of Unreason does not feature Contract, as far as I remember. Though, to make the reason why iron affects Gentry congruent with my wider 'metaplot', I decided they made a contract with 'The World' (also known as Gaia and under other names, depending whom you ask). Before Gentry could only snatch people veering off into Hedge. Gaia needed another supernatural threat (she spawned one of Kindred Clan progenitors) that would prey on humanity so they don't stagnate in their ways, but she felt that just letting Gentry in would be dull and they needed a clear disadvantage to level the playing field a bit, so she cursed them with vulnerability to Earth's Blood aka iron, a metal associated with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T13:15:09-07:00","id":289918,"title":"","content":"I was going with the corebook, but I looked up that legend and follow your thoughts better now.<br /> <br /> I stick to my position on magnetism unless the source is magic. That type of iron demagnetizes over time. I would nix welding as it would seem to defy the spirit of the rules for that legend. Rivets would work well enough instead. FYI the temperature required to mess up the iron would be 900 C. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}